I'll use Floyd's cycle detection algorithm. First, I use slow and fast pointers, moving one and two steps respectively. If they meet, a cycle exists. Then I reset slow to the head and move both pointers one step at a time. The node where they meet again is the beginning of the cycle. If fast reaches null, there is no cycle.
